{
  "slug": "artist:dj-paul-elstak",
  "name": "DJ Paul Elstak",
  "editorial_article": "Born in The Hague in 1966, DJ Paul Elstak is a foundational architect of Dutch gabber, mainstream hardcore, and happy hardcore. He launched Offensive Records in 2001 to distinguish his output, marking a departure from his early alias-based approach where he used 'Paul Elstak' for happy hardcore and 'DJ Paul' for gabber productions. His career highlights include the 1995 release of 'Rainbow in the Sky' and a 2024 production credit on Joost Klein’s Eurovision entry 'Europapa'. Recent efforts have seen him bridge generational gaps in the scene, including a 2024 collaboration with techno artist Reinier Zonneveld on 'XTCWTF' via the label Filth On Acid. In 2025, he revisited his own catalog, releasing a reimagined version of his 1997 classic 'Luv U More' alongside Scooter and Joost Klein.",
